WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.380
- All right, y'all, before we go,

00:00:01.380 --> 00:00:03.750
let's take a quick dive into
the world of social media.

00:00:03.750 --> 00:00:06.449
This is "What I'm Liking".
(upbeat jazzy music)

00:00:06.449 --> 00:00:07.890
(audience cheers)

00:00:07.890 --> 00:00:10.050
The holidays can be mostly magical,

00:00:10.050 --> 00:00:12.030
but for some of us, extra time with family

00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:14.220
means a few extra curse words.

00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:15.510
It happen.

00:00:15.510 --> 00:00:17.999
That's where Auntie Bev comes in.

00:00:17.999 --> 00:00:19.500
(Kelly laughs)
This former journalist

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:21.600
and educator started a TikTok channel

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:23.400
teaching vocabulary words.

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:26.490
She's encouraging everyone
to curse with class

00:00:26.490 --> 00:00:27.810
this holiday season.

00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:29.070
Nice.
(air wisps)

00:00:29.070 --> 00:00:31.161
- So, you wanna call somebody a ho,

00:00:31.161 --> 00:00:33.510
(audience laughs)
they're licentious.

00:00:33.510 --> 00:00:35.160
You wanna call somebody a (beep),

00:00:36.450 --> 00:00:40.230
they are viragos or termagants.

00:00:40.230 --> 00:00:43.410
If you wanna call a man a ho,
(Auntie Bev laughs)

00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:46.500
'cause there's some
male hos out there, too.

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:51.420
Those can be either louts,
L-O-U-T or lotharios.

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:53.427
You're just a lothario.

00:00:53.427 --> 00:00:56.520
(audience cheers)
- I love her!

00:00:56.520 --> 00:00:58.200
Let's get Auntie Bev in here!

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:02.010
She's watching on WRAL
TV in Raleigh-Durham.

00:01:02.010 --> 00:01:03.907
What's up?
(audience cheers)

00:01:03.907 --> 00:01:07.290
- Hey, Kelly! Hi, how are you?

00:01:07.290 --> 00:01:10.800
- Oh my... I am obsessed with
you, I'm gonna lead with that.

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:12.063
I do know some louts.

00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:16.530
So you're trying to help
at Christmas time, right?

00:01:16.530 --> 00:01:19.560
- Absolutely, because I
don't know about your family,

00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:22.590
but let me tell you about my family.

00:01:22.590 --> 00:01:25.140
Full disclosure here.
(Auntie Bev laughs)

00:01:25.140 --> 00:01:27.990
We have those family members who come over

00:01:27.990 --> 00:01:31.650
and, you know, they've
already had a lot to drink.

00:01:31.650 --> 00:01:32.970
- [Kelly] Oh.
- And they come over

00:01:32.970 --> 00:01:35.130
and they have more eggnog

00:01:35.130 --> 00:01:37.380
and they just become totally obnoxious

00:01:37.380 --> 00:01:39.390
and you wanna bite your tongue

00:01:39.390 --> 00:01:42.630
because you know you
want to cuss them out.

00:01:42.630 --> 00:01:43.650
Not curse them out-
- Yeah.

00:01:43.650 --> 00:01:46.443
- [Auntie Bev] Because
cursing is the formality.

00:01:46.443 --> 00:01:49.171
Cuss them out is the hood version.

00:01:49.171 --> 00:01:50.004
(audience laughs)

00:01:50.004 --> 00:01:53.310
So, when you want to cuss them out,

00:01:53.310 --> 00:01:55.230
you call them a lummox.

00:01:55.230 --> 00:01:58.350
Just ask them to just stop being a lummox.

00:01:58.350 --> 00:01:59.730
We don't need that.

00:01:59.730 --> 00:02:01.770
So, what do you want to tell Grandma

00:02:01.770 --> 00:02:04.147
as opposed to just being
upset and saying, you know,

00:02:04.147 --> 00:02:07.020
"Grandma, you need to
sit your (censored) down

00:02:07.020 --> 00:02:08.640
and shut up."
(audience laughs)

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:11.760
Say, "Grandma, this is your day.

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:14.190
You don't need to be a harridan."

00:02:14.190 --> 00:02:18.720
Now, a harridan is a bossy, strict,

00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:20.931
old, belligerent woman.

00:02:20.931 --> 00:02:22.350
(audience laughs)

00:02:22.350 --> 00:02:23.500
Instead of saying that-
- Oh my God!

00:02:23.500 --> 00:02:27.300
- You just say, "Grandma,
don't be a harridan."

00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:31.200
And then you have the
male cousins who come over

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:33.150
and they're hitting on everybody

00:02:33.150 --> 00:02:36.339
until they realize you're their cousin.

00:02:36.339 --> 00:02:37.800
(audience laughs)

00:02:37.800 --> 00:02:40.147
They're lotharios, so you just say,

00:02:40.147 --> 00:02:42.120
"Hey, look, lothario.

00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:42.953
I'm your cousin!

00:02:42.953 --> 00:02:45.630
I'm your sister's niece."

00:02:45.630 --> 00:02:47.250
So you have to come up with

00:02:47.250 --> 00:02:50.267
a lot of different classier words-

00:02:50.267 --> 00:02:52.080
- [Kelly] I like it.
- In order to say

00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:55.050
the same kinds of things you would say

00:02:55.050 --> 00:02:58.091
when you're using the four,
five-letter nasty words.

00:02:58.091 --> 00:02:59.401
(audience applauds)
- [Kelly] Yes.

00:02:59.401 --> 00:03:03.570
Here's the thing, I wish that
I were spending Christmas

00:03:03.570 --> 00:03:06.660
with you because you are hysterical,

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:08.460
I like the words, I like it.

00:03:08.460 --> 00:03:09.690
Sometimes you need the real ones,

00:03:09.690 --> 00:03:12.570
but try and keep it classy, America, okay?

00:03:12.570 --> 00:03:14.430
Thank you so much, Auntie Bev!
(audience cheers)

00:03:14.430 --> 00:03:15.870
I'm liking your post right now!

00:03:15.870 --> 00:03:16.703
(alert dings)
(audience cheers)

00:03:16.703 --> 00:03:17.760
That's not all, though.

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:19.530
Our season-long partner Pilot,

00:03:19.530 --> 00:03:21.577
pen-makers of Precise, the go-to pen of

00:03:21.577 --> 00:03:23.580
"The Kelly Clarkson Show"
want to celebrate people

00:03:23.580 --> 00:03:26.310
who make the holidays a little
less dramatic and more fun,

00:03:26.310 --> 00:03:27.143
and that is you, ma'am.

00:03:27.143 --> 00:03:28.860
So they're giving you $1,000.

00:03:28.860 --> 00:03:32.203
How's that sound?
(audience cheers)

00:03:34.868 --> 00:03:35.701
Thank you so much, Auntie Bev!

00:03:37.171 --> 00:03:39.353
Have such a great holiday season!

